## Feature #7 Increment 1 (spec §4.7) — deterministic virtual `TestClock`: a
## `--test`-style mode where the per-thread reactor swaps its real OS timer for
## an in-memory virtual clock. `TestClock.install` returns a guard (its `def
## drop` restores the real clock); `TestClock.advance(d)` jumps virtual time
## forward, firing every due timer + waking its parked task. So a long
## `Async.sleep` resolves INSTANTLY when the clock is advanced past it — no real
## sleep. This is the killer property: "register a long timeout, advance past it,
## assert it fired — in milliseconds."
##
## Mechanism (in virtual mode): `ruxen_time_now_ns` returns the virtual now, so
## the sleep's deadline is virtual; `register_timer` records the timer in the
## reactor's slot list WITHOUT arming a real timerfd/kevent (same handle ABI);
## `advance(d)` bumps virtual-now + marks every timer with `deadline <= now`
## fired + wakes it; `park_current` returns immediately (no `epoll_wait(-1)`).
##
## Drive: hand-poll the sleep once (it registers a virtual timer for 60s and
## parks), `advance` 60s (fires it), poll again (Ready). REAL wall-clock around
## the whole thing must be tiny (<< 60s) — measured via a SECOND, real (non-
## virtual)... no: we assert by COMPLETING under the harness cap. A 60s real
## sleep would time out; finishing fast proves the advance fired it virtually.
## We print the poll outcomes to prove the exact sequence.

use std.time.Duration

def main
  puts "clock start"
  var guard = TestClock.install
  var cx = Context.executor

  # The sleep: 60 seconds of VIRTUAL time. Its first poll registers a virtual
  # timer and parks (Pending). A real 60s sleep would hang the harness.
  var s = Async.sleep(Duration.from_secs(60))

  match (&var s).poll(&var cx)
    Poll.Ready(_) -> puts "poll1=ready (BUG: should park first)"
    Poll.Pending  -> puts "poll1=pending"
  end

  # Advance virtual time PAST the deadline → fires the parked timer.
  TestClock.advance(Duration.from_secs(60))

  match (&var s).poll(&var cx)
    Poll.Ready(_) -> puts "poll2=ready"
    Poll.Pending  -> puts "poll2=pending (BUG: advance should have fired it)"
  end

  puts "clock done"
end
